# Git workflow (Vectra)

Canonical detail: [docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md](docs/desarrollo-git-openspec.md).

## Branches

- **`main`**: stable line; do not commit directly unless the user explicitly asks.
- **`develop`**: integration branch; **create all work branches from `develop`**.
- **Work branch name**: `T-XX-YY-ZZ` only (no `feature/` prefix). Same name as the OpenSpec change.

## Flow

1. Update `develop`, then `git checkout -b T-XX-YY-ZZ`.
2. One OpenSpec change = one spec = one branch.
3. Merge into **`develop`** via Pull Request (target `develop`, not `main`).
4. Updates to **`main`** come from `develop` at each course delivery or hito, followed by an annotated SemVer tag (see doc § 10).
5. No HU branches (`develop → hu → spec` is not used); HUs are tracked with GitHub issues and milestones (doc § 11).

## Ticket traceability

- `T-XX-YY` = ticket in [docs/7-tickets.md](docs/7-tickets.md).
- `ZZ` = spec index within that ticket (`01`, `02`, …).
